PART C.  V2-V3.  THE 'SYSTEMATIC' IS A GEOMETRY FACTOR BETWEEN TWO KNOWN QUANTITIES, NOT AN AMBIGUITY.
==========================================================================================================================
  The sphere average and FM12 eq.60 use the SAME theory, the SAME nu, the SAME a_0 and the SAME masses.
  This script SET OUT to show FM12 eq.60 is a directional slice of the exact field -- its along-the-axis
  value -- so that the difference would be a pure geometry factor.  The measured answer is different and
  STRONGER against the claim, and is reported as measured: at nearly every object FM12 eq.60 falls BELOW
  the exact QUMOND field at EVERY polar angle, so it is not any component of the exact solution at all.
