  Test 2, the analytic version.  In the external-field-dominated limit the exact angle average is
  nu(x_e)(1 + L_e/3) x_i (Milgrom 1986, ApJ 302, 617) and the one-dimensional formula tends to
  nu(x_e)(1 + L_e) x_i, so the ratio is the fixed number (1 + L_e/3)/(1 + L_e) with L_e = dln nu/dln x.
